{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/blog/2010-10-10-mvc-binding-restriction/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"html":"<p>There are a few options when restricting what properties of a type get automatically bound by the framework.</p>\n<p>Take the Loler type seen in my other MVC2 blog posts.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"csharp\"><pre style=\"counter-reset: linenumber NaN\" class=\"language-csharp line-numbers\"><code class=\"language-csharp\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token attribute\"><span class=\"token class-name\">Bind</span><span class=\"token attribute-arguments\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>Include<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"ID,Name,Description\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span></span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">Loler</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n<span class=\"token comment\">//entity framework generated</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"line-numbers-rows\" style=\"white-space: normal; width: auto; left: 0;\"><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></pre></div>\n<p>Notice only the ID, Name and Description properties will be bound by the MVC Framework.</p>\n<p>Per Usage restriction</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"csharp\"><pre style=\"counter-reset: linenumber NaN\" class=\"language-csharp line-numbers\"><code class=\"language-csharp\"><span class=\"token function\">UpdateModel</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>loler<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\